erates, causing it to register a dynamic workflow/node-scoped path instead of the intended static one. Root-caused by inspecting n8n's own webhook_entity table directly. Fixed by generating a real UUID and committing it in workflows/invoice-intake.json."}, {"id": "oidc_audience_mapper_fix", "label": "oidc-audience-mapper protocol mapper fix (Keycloak 26 omits aud)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/reports/sprint-6.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Keycloak 26 omits aud by default. fleet_api/auth.py already tolerates this via azp, but oauth2-proxy has no such fallback. Fixed at the source with an explicit oidc-audience-mapper protocol mapper on the n8n Keycloak client, not a workaround flag."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_reports_sprint_6", "target": "docs_reports_sprint_6_task_6_1", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/reports/sprint-6.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_reports_sprint_6", "target": "docs_reports_sprint_6_task_6_2", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/reports/sprint-6.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_reports_sprint_6", "target": "docs_reports_sprint_6_task_6_3", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/reports/sprint-6.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_reports_sprint_6_task_6_1", "target": "infra_compose_docker_compose_dev_n8n_oauth2_proxy", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/reports/sprint-6.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_reports_sprint_6_task_6_1", "target": "fleet_api_key_service_concept", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file"